# The pass that names the optional mods: a body retexture drawn without legs, and something that
# fills wornGraphicPath. Select it with `Run-PickleWsl.ps1 -DepMap wsl-deps.wdi-ab.map`.
# One line per mod: packageId then its Workshop id.
#
# WDI and AB carry the captures rather than decorate them. Without a body retexture drawn without
# legs there is no defect to photograph; with nothing filling wornGraphicPath the pawn renders bare,
# because vanilla Apparel_Pants has no worn graphic of its own. AB also needs its settings file to
# do anything at all: see config/wdi-ab/.
wdi.realistic.bodies   3527486510
ab.vplrf               2986402536

# astryl.tailormade is not listed here: it is a hard dependency of the mod, and its Workshop id
# lives in wsl-ids.map, which every pass reads. Listing it here staged it twice.

# The inspect-tab steps 02-gear-tab.feature needs, as a PickleTools package on the stock Pickle
# rather than through -PickleSrc: see wsl-deps.tools.map, which carries the same line for the bare pass.
nelim.pickletools.inspecttabs   path:PickleTools/InspectTabs/Mod
